  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AHRN Empowering grassroot movements</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The mission of the AHRN fund is to support and empower grassroot movements or individual activists who work and/or are part of marginalized groups, particularly women, LGBTQI and indigenous communities, to have a voice in decision-making processes related to environmental issues and advocate for policies that prioritize their needs. The goal is to create a sustainable, equitable, inclusive and just society that values the interdependence of all living beings and the natural environment, by addressing theintersectionality of environmental issues and social justice. The fund aims to make a real impact on the lives of these marginalized communities by providing resources and support to help them advocate for their rights and well-being. Our fund aims to support projects and initiatives led by young feminist women that promote sustainable development, clean energy, and conservation of natural resources. We believein the power of grassroot young women-led solutions and we prioritize funding opportunities that involve empowering grassroot feminists in Africa. Additionally, we will focus on supporting education and awareness programs that educate people about the importance of environmental stewardship and the impact of our actions on the planet. Therefore thevision of this fund is to create a world where all people have equal access to the benefits of a healthy environment and a sustainable future.</narrative>
  </description>
