  <result aggregation-status="1" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate justice activism-Strength CS</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSOs have strengthened capacity (and maintain and expand their civic space) to engage local, nationally and internationally in influencing on gendered climate justice, natural resources and/or land rights issues in an effective and inclusive way.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">9920-1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSOs who demonstrate strengthened capacity to engage in influencing</narrative>
    </description>
    <reference code="9920-1" indicator-uri="https://oxfam.box.com/s/2l7ktb7otlfcoflkmqp9gp4eg68oexgn" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline iso-date="2023-06-01" value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <actual value="10">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">These include:1. Ecobed Biotech Brand &#x2013; Uganda: Training of women farmers in sustainable agro-practices, including transforming food waste into products such as organic fertilizer, animal feed and mosquito repellant, and training in Black Soldier Fly Larvae farming. Used this to raise awareness about malaria prevention.

2. Parker&apos;s Mobile Clinic &#x2013; Nigeria: Equitable access to resilient healthcare for women in underserved and marginalized communities by addressing healthcare gaps through outreach programs, partnerships, and digital innovations. Three virtual webinars on the connections between climate change and health.

3. Initiatives pour le D&#xe9;veloppement et l&#x2019;inclusion Sociale (IDIS-ONG) - Benin: &#x201c;Safe Nature, Safe People&quot; project successfully carried out a series of activities aimed at restoring the mangrove ecosystems in Akokponawa, Benin, with significant community involvement.

4. Gifted Community Centre &#x2013; Kenya: Training for women with disabilities on food security and climate justice.

5. Women Initiatives &#x2013; Lesotho: climate change awareness and promoting upcyling

6. Wanania Green &#x2013; Comoros: skills training on green jobs for women.

7. GDA Pure Nature &#x2013; Tunisia: Sustainable Waste Management and Soil Enrichment for Aromatic and Medicinal Plants project.

8. Students&#x2019; Movement for Climate Justice (SM4CJ) - Tanzania: initiative focused on leadership development, capacity-building, and practical environmental engagement.

9. Golden Waste Solution &#x2013; Liberia: The project aimed at promoting sustainable waste management and gender equity.

10. Femme Au Cerveau Vert Pour L&#x2019;avenir Assume &#x2013; Democratic Republic of the Congo: The project was implemented in Goma and its surrounding camps, aimed to promote sustainable environmental practicesand empower displaced women and girls affected by conflict.</narrative>
      </comment>
